# The committed PDFs are binary: never normalise line endings in them, or a
# clone under core.autocrlf=true would see a corrupted file and the byte
# reproducibility test would fail for a reason that has nothing to do with the
# renderer. Week 01 hit exactly this with an exported seed file.
*.pdf binary

# LaTeX source is text and is read by pdflatex on both platforms; pin it to LF
# so the paper builds identically either side of the CRLF boundary.
*.tex text eol=lf
